edia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cutlery_designed_by_Zaha_Hadid_for_company_WMF%2C_2007_N.3.jpg/1280px-Cutlery_designed_by_Zaha_Hadid_for_company_WMF%2C_2007_N.3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cutlery_designed_by_Zaha_Hadid_for_company_WMF%2C_2007_N.3.jpg/500px-Cutlery_designed_by_Zaha_Hadid_for_company_WMF%2C_2007_N.3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cutlery designed by architect and designer Zaha Hadid (2007). The slightly oblique end part of the fork and the spoons, as well as the knife handle, are examples of designing for both aesthetic form and practical function.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACutlery_designed_by_Zaha_Hadid_for_company_WMF%2C_2007_N.3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Y-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg/500px-Y-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Y-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg/1280px-Y-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Y-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg/500px-Y-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early concept design sketches by the architect Erling Viksjø, exploring the relationships between existing and proposed new buildings","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AY-blokken_som_plassvegg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Bar%C3%A9nyi_B%C3%A9la-biztons%C3%A1gi_fejleszt%C3%A9s.jpg/500px-Bar%C3%A9nyi_B%C3%A9la-biztons%C3%A1gi_fejleszt%C3%A9s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail